S1 → S2)|, |∂(S2 → S1)|)`, an upper bound\n    on `pw(G[S1 ∪ S2])` for disjoint `S1`, `S2`; `pw_of(S)` returns `pw(G[S])`.\"\"\"\n    b1 = boundary_to(adj, S1, S2).bit_count()\n    b2 = boundary_to(adj, S2, S1).bit_count()\n    return max(pw_of(S1), pw_of(S2)) + min(b1, b2)\n\n\ndef bisection_bound(adj: list[int], tree, pw_of, use_max: bool = False) -> tuple[int, list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"`BisectionTree G S bs k` of `CutLemma.lean` evaluated on a concrete tree:\n    `tree` is a mask (a leaf) or a pair `(left, right)` of trees on disjoint\n    masks; returns `(k, bs)` with `k` the largest leaf pathwidth and `bs[i]` the\n    largest `min(|∂₁|, |∂₂|)` (or `max`, with `use_max`) over the splits at depth\n    `i`; the theorem gives `pw(G[S]) ≤ k + sum(bs)` (and `≤ k + 2 sum(bs)` for the\n    max form, the item's C2).\"\"\"\n    levels: list[int] = []\n    leaves: list[int] = []\n\n    def mask_of(t) -> int:\n        return t if isinstance(t, int) else mask_of(t[0]) | mask_of(t[1])\n\n    def walk(t, depth: int) -> None:\n        if isinstance(t, int):\n            leaves.append(pw_of(t))\n            return\n        S1, S2 = mask_of(t[0]), mask_of(t[1])\n        if S1 & S2:\n            raise ValueError(\"the two sides of a split must be disjoint\")\n        b1 = boundary_to(adj, S1, S2).bit_count()\n        b2 = boundary_to(adj, S2, S1).bit_count()\n        b = max(b1, b2) if use_max else min(b1, b2)\n        while len(levels) <= depth:\n            levels.append(0)\n        levels[depth] = max(levels[depth], b)\n        walk(t[0], depth + 1)\n        walk(t[1], depth + 1)\n\n    walk(tree, 0)\n    return max(leaves), levels\n'''\nopen(p, \"w\").write(s)\nEOF\nmkdir -p reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/04_cut && python3 -c \"\nfrom learning.edwards_mcdermid import parse_g6, boundary_to, separator_cut_bound, bisection_bound, pathwidth_induced\nn, adj = parse_g6('F]~vo')\nprint(n, adj, boundary_to(adj, 0b0001111, 0b1110000))\npw = lambda S: pathwidth_induced(adj, S)\nprint(separator_cut_bound(adj, 0b0001111, 0b1110000, pw), pw(127))\nprint(bisection_bound(adj, ((0b0000011, 0b0001100), (0b0110000, 0b1000000)), pw))\n\"","description":"Add item-04 helpers to the Python module and smoke-test them"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":749,"cache_read_input_tokens":149863,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":749,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":16,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9391627-7973-489b-a3e2-64b9c429644d","uuid":"803d673e-b04d-418b-8193-c515a0b6db74","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:29:52.894Z","request_id":"req_011CgdKAx5k7G4pixTpLQ16T","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_0152AydPAiXwudoJkzYHvwxK":{"command":"cd /home/al/dev/MOSP && python3 - <<'EOF'\nimport re\np = \"learning/edwards_mcdermid.py\"\ns = open(p).read()\ns = s.replace('''    \"paper_choice\", \"algorithm_x\", \"pathwidth_induced\",\n]''', '''    \"paper_choice\", \"algorithm_x\", \"pathwidth_induced\",\n    # item 04: the cut lemma (`CutLemma.lean`) on bit masks\n    \"parse_g6\", \"boundary_to\", \"separator_cut_bound\", \"bisection_bound\",\n]''')\ns += '''\n\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n# item 04: the cut lemma and its iterated form, as `DegreeBound/CutLemma.lean`\n# states them (`reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §4)\n# ----------------------------------------------------------------------------\n\n\ndef parse_g6(line: str) -> tuple[int, list[int]]:\n    \"\"\"A graph6 line (`nauty-geng` output) as `(n, adjacency bit masks)`.\"\"\"\n    b = line.strip().encode()\n    n = b[0] - 63\n    bitlist: list[int] = []\n    for ch in b[1:]:\n        v = ch - 63\n        bitlist += [(v >> i) & 1 for i in range(5, -1, -1)]\n    adj = [0] * n\n  