{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgdKFhK7qQqa2DSYvizEX","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018Udf7t4cytsh5QxbTxENeW","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/CutLemma.lean <<'EOF'\n/-\nCopyright (c) 2026 Alexandre Linhares. All rights reserved.\nReleased under the MIT license as described in the file LICENSE.\n\n# The cut lemma and its iterated form\n\nItem 04 of loop0012 (`reports/edwards_mcdermid_plan.md` §0.4 (3), §0.5;\n`reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §2.1 (2) and §4): the one-cut transfer — a vertex\npartition with its two boundaries bounds the pathwidth of the whole by the\npathwidths of the two sides — and its recursive iteration. Neither depends on\nthe two named hypotheses of the Edwards–McDermid formalisation\n(`CubicPathwidthBound`, `ReductionPathwidthBound`, item 09); both are tools for\nevery graph.\n\n* `boundaryTo G A B` — the vertices of `A` with a neighbour in `B`;\n  `boundary G A` — the vertices of `A` with a neighbour outside `A`\n  (`boundary_eq_boundaryTo_compl`).\n* `pathwidth_induce_mono` — `T ⊆ U → pathwidth G[T] ≤ pathwidth G[U]`.\n* `pathwidth_induce_le_induce_add_card_sdiff` — `T ⊆ U → pathwidth G[U] ≤ pathwidth G[T] + |U ∖ T|`,\n  the relative form of `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl` (`TreeBound.lean`).\n* `pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_boundaryTo` — for disjoint `S₁`, `S₂`,\n  `pathwidth G[S₁ ∪ S₂] ≤ max (pathwidth G[S₁]) (pathwidth G[S₂]) + |∂(S₁ → S₂)|`:\n  delete the boundary (the lemma above), the rest is a disjoint union with no edge\n  between the sides (`pathwidth_induce_union_le_max`), and `G[S₁ ∖ ∂] ≤ G[S₁]`.\n* **C1s** `pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_min` (relative) and\n  `pathwidth_le_max_add_min_boundary` (global): the separator form\n  `pathwidth G ≤ max (pathwidth G[S]) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ]) + min |∂S| |∂Sᶜ|`.\n* **C1** `pathwidth_le_cut`: the item's three-term form\n  `pathwidth G ≤ max (max (pathwidth G[S] + |∂S|) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ] + |∂Sᶜ|)) (|∂S| + |∂Sᶜ| − 1)`,\n  a corollary of C1s (`max a b + min c d ≤ max (a + c) (b + d)`); stated as the\n  item asks, with the `− 1` in `ℕ`.\n* **C2s** `BisectionTree G S bs k` — a recursive bisection of `S` given level by level:\n  `bs = []` means `pathwidth G[S] ≤ k`; `bs = b :: bs'` means `S` splits into two\n  disjoint parts whose smaller boundary (`min`) has at most `b` vertices, each part\n  carrying a `BisectionTree` for `bs'`. `pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTree`:\n  `BisectionTree G univ bs k → pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum`; by induction on `bs` through\n  the relative C1s, so it never needs a nested `induce`.\n* **C2** `BisectionTreeMax` is the same with the larger boundary (`max`) budgeted, as the\n  item's text has it; it implies `BisectionTree` (`bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax`),\n  and `pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax_two_mul` is the item's `pathwidth G ≤ k + 2 bs.sum`\n  (the factor 2 is slack: `pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax` has `k + bs.sum`).\n\n**What these lemmas do not give.** Fomin & Høie (2006) reach `pw ≤ (1/6 + ε) n` for\ncubic graphs with **one** level — a Monien–Preis bisection with at most `(1/6 + ε/2) n`\ncut edges, their Lemma 4 on each side (a path decomposition of a graph of maximum degree\n3 of width at most `max{|X|, n/3 + 1} + (2/3) log₃ n + 1` whose *last* bag is a\nprescribed set `X`), and a sweep across the boundary that holds the middle bags at\n`|∂V₁| + 1` — not by iterating C2: iterating C2s with Monien–Preis cuts of `(1/6 + ε)`\nof each piece sums to `n/3`. Lemma 4 and the sweep are stated in\n`reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §4 and are not proved here.\n\nEvery statement was checked by brute force before it was stated\n(`reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/04_cut/check.py`): the relative forms on every\nordered pair of disjoint vertex sets of every graph to 7 vertices, the global forms on\nevery partition, the bisection forms on 2,000 random graphs at 10–12 vertices.\n-/\nimport MOSPFormalization.TreeBound\nimport MOSPFormalization.Minor\n\nset_option linter.unusedSectionVars false\n\nnamespace MOSPFormalization\n\nvariable {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\nvariable (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n\n/-! ### Boundaries -/\n\n/-- The vertices of `A` with a neighbour in `B`. -/\ndef boundaryTo (A B : Finset V) : Finset V := A.filter (fun a => ∃ b ∈ B, G.Adj a b)\n\n/-- The boundary of `A`: the vertices of `A` with a neighbour outside `A`. -/\ndef boundary (A : Finset V) : Finset V := A.filter (fun a => ∃ b, b ∉ A ∧ G.Adj a b)\n\ntheorem boundaryTo_subset (A B : Finset V) : boundaryTo G A B ⊆ A := Finset.filter_subset _ _\n\ntheorem boundary_subset (A : Finset V) : boundary G A ⊆ A := Finset.filter_subset _ _\n\ntheorem mem_boundaryTo {A B : Finset V} {a : V} :\n    a ∈ boundaryTo G A B ↔ a ∈ A ∧ ∃ b ∈ B, G.Adj a b := Finset.mem_filter\n\ntheorem mem_boundary {A : Finset V} {a : V} :\n    a ∈ boundary G A ↔ a ∈ A ∧ ∃ b, b ∉ A ∧ G.Adj a b := Finset.mem_filter\n\n/-- The boundary of `A` is its boundary towards the complement. -/\ntheorem boundary_eq_boundaryTo_compl (A : Finset V) : boundary G A = boundaryTo G A Aᶜ := by\n  ext a\n  simp [mem_boundary, mem_boundaryTo]\n\n/-- No edge leaves `A ∖ ∂(A → B)` for `B`. -/\ntheorem not_adj_of_mem_sdiff_boundaryTo {A B : Finset V} {a b : V}\n    (ha : a ∈ A \\ boundaryTo G A B) (hb : b ∈ B) : ¬ G.Adj a b := fun h =>\n  (Finset.mem_sdiff.mp ha).2 ((mem_boundaryTo G).mpr ⟨(Finset.mem_sdiff.mp ha).1, b, hb, h⟩)\n\n/-! ### Induced subgraphs of induced subgraphs -/\n\n/-- Monotonicity under vertex inclusion: `T ⊆ U → pathwidth G[T] ≤ pathwidth G[U]`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_mono {T U : Finset V} (h : T ⊆ U) :\n    pathwidth (G.induce (↑T : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (G.induce (↑U : Set V)) :=\n  pathwidth_le_of_injective (G.induceHomOfLE (Finset.coe_subset.mpr h)).toHom\n    (G.induceHomOfLE (Finset.coe_subset.mpr h)).injective\n\n/-- The pathwidth of `G` is that of `G[univ]`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_univ : pathwidth (G.induce (↑(Finset.univ : Finset V) : Set V)) = pathwidth G := by\n  rw [Finset.coe_univ]\n  exact pathwidth_eq_of_iso (SimpleGraph.induceUnivIso G)\n\n/-- The relative deletion lemma: `T ⊆ U → pathwidth G[U] ≤ pathwidth G[T] + |U ∖ T|`\n(`pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl` applied inside `G[U]`). -/\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_le_induce_add_card_sdiff {T U : Finset V} (h : T ⊆ U) :\n    pathwidth (G.induce (↑U : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (G.induce (↑T : Set V)) + (U \\ T).card := by\n  -- the vertices of `G[U]` that lie in `T`\n  let S : Finset (↑(↑U : Set V)) := Finset.univ.filter (fun x => x.val ∈ T)\n  have h1 := pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl (G.induce (↑U : Set V)) S\n  -- `G[U][S]` embeds in `G[T]`\n  have h2 : pathwidth ((G.induce (↑U : Set V)).induce (↑S : Set ↑(↑U : Set V))) ≤\n      pathwidth (G.induce (↑T : Set V)) := by\n    refine pathwidth_le_of_injective\n      (⟨fun x => ⟨x.val.val, (Finset.mem_filter.mp (Finset.mem_coe.mp x.2)).2⟩,\n        fun {x y} hxy => hxy⟩ : (G.induce (↑U : Set V)).induce (↑S : Set ↑(↑U : Set V)) →g\n          G.induce (↑T : Set V)) ?_\n    intro x y hxy\n    exact Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext (congrArg Subtype.val hxy))\n  -- the complement of `S` in `G[U]` injects into `U ∖ T`\n  have h3 : Sᶜ.card ≤ (U \\ T).card := by\n    refine Finset.card_le_card_of_injOn (fun x => x.val) ?_ Subtype.val_injective.injOn\n    intro x hx\n    have hx' := Finset.mem_compl.mp hx\n    simp only [S, Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and] at hx'\n    exact Finset.mem_sdiff.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_coe.mp x.2, hx'⟩\n  omega\n\n/-! ### C1s: the separator form of the cut lemma -/\n\n/-- One side of the cut lemma: for disjoint `S₁`, `S₂`,\n`pathwidth G[S₁ ∪ S₂] ≤ max (pathwidth G[S₁]) (pathwidth G[S₂]) + |∂(S₁ → S₂)|`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_boundaryTo (S₁ S₂ : Finset V) (hd : Disjoint S₁ S₂) :\n    pathwidth (G.induce (↑(S₁ ∪ S₂) : Set V)) ≤\n      max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₁ : Set V))) (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₂ : Set V))) +\n        (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card := by\n  set B := boundaryTo G S₁ S₂ with hB\n  set T := (S₁ \\ B) ∪ S₂ with hT\n  have hTU : T ⊆ S₁ ∪ S₂ :=\n    Finset.union_subset_union Finset.sdiff_subset (Finset.Subset.refl _)\n  -- delete the boundary: at most `|B|` vertices\n  have h1 := pathwidth_induce_le_induce_add_card_sdiff G hTU\n  have hcard : ((S₁ ∪ S₂) \\ T).card ≤ B.card := by\n    apply Finset.card_le_card\n    intro x hx\n    simp only [hT, Finset.mem_sdiff, Finset.mem_union, not_or, not_and, not_not] at hx\n    rcases hx.1 with h | h\n    · exact hx.2.1 h\n    · exact absurd h hx.2.2\n  -- the rest is a disjoint union with no edge between the sides\n  have h2 : pathwidth (G.induce (↑T : Set V)) ≤\n      max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑(S₁ \\ B) : Set V))) (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₂ : Set V))) :=\n    pathwidth_induce_union_le_max G (S₁ \\ B) S₂\n      (Finset.disjoint_of_subset_left Finset.sdiff_subset hd)\n      (fun a ha b hb => not_adj_of_mem_sdiff_boundaryTo G ha hb)\n  have h3 : pathwidth (G.induce (↑(S₁ \\ B) : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₁ : Set V)) :=\n    pathwidth_induce_mono G Finset.sdiff_subset\n  omega\n\n/-- **C1s, relative form.** For disjoint `S₁`, `S₂`,\n`pathwidth G[S₁ ∪ S₂] ≤ max (pathwidth G[S₁]) (pathwidth G[S₂]) + min |∂(S₁ → S₂)| |∂(S₂ → S₁)|`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_min (S₁ S₂ : Finset V) (hd : Disjoint S₁ S₂) :\n    pathwidth (G.induce (↑(S₁ ∪ S₂) : Set V)) ≤\n      max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₁ : Set V))) (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₂ : Set V))) +\n        min (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card (boundaryTo G S₂ S₁).card := by\n  have h1 := pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_boundaryTo G S₁ S₂ hd\n  have h2 := pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_boundaryTo G S₂ S₁ hd.symm\n  rw [Finset.union_comm] at h2\n  omega\n\n/-- **C1s.** `pathwidth G ≤ max (pathwidth G[S]) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ]) + min |∂S| |∂Sᶜ|`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_le_max_add_min_boundary (S : Finset V) :\n    pathwidth G ≤\n      max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V))) (pathwidth (G.induce (↑Sᶜ : Set V))) +\n        min (boundary G S).card (boundary G Sᶜ).card := by\n  have h := pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_min G S Sᶜ Finset.disjoint_compl_right\n  rw [Finset.union_compl, pathwidth_induce_univ] at h\n  rw [boundary_eq_boundaryTo_compl, boundary_eq_boundaryTo_compl, compl_compl]\n  exact h\n\n/-- **C1**, the item's three-term form:\n`pathwidth G ≤ max (max (pathwidth G[S] + |∂S|) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ] + |∂Sᶜ|)) (|∂S| + |∂Sᶜ| − 1)`.\nThe last term is never the binding one; it is kept because Fomin & Høie's\n`P₁, P₂, P₃` construction has it. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_le_cut (S : Finset V) :\n    pathwidth G ≤\n      max (max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) + (boundary G S).card)\n               (pathwidth (G.induce (↑Sᶜ : Set V)) + (boundary G Sᶜ).card))\n          ((boundary G S).card + (boundary G Sᶜ).card - 1) := by\n  have h := pathwidth_le_max_add_min_boundary G S\n  omega\n\n/-! ### C2: the iterated form -/\n\n/-- A recursive bisection of `S`, level by level: `BisectionTree G S [] k` says\n`pathwidth G[S] ≤ k`; `BisectionTree G S (b :: bs) k` says `S` is the disjoint union of\ntwo parts whose smaller boundary has at most `b` vertices, each a `BisectionTree` for\n`bs`. -/\ndef BisectionTree : Finset V → List ℕ → ℕ → Prop\n  | S, [], k => pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) ≤ k\n  | S, b :: bs, k => ∃ S₁ S₂ : Finset V, S₁ ∪ S₂ = S ∧ Disjoint S₁ S₂ ∧\n      min (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card (boundaryTo G S₂ S₁).card ≤ b ∧\n      BisectionTree S₁ bs k ∧ BisectionTree S₂ bs k\n\n/-- The same with the larger boundary budgeted at each split (the item's C2). -/\ndef BisectionTreeMax : Finset V → List ℕ → ℕ → Prop\n  | S, [], k => pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) ≤ k\n  | S, b :: bs, k => ∃ S₁ S₂ : Finset V, S₁ ∪ S₂ = S ∧ Disjoint S₁ S₂ ∧\n      max (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card (boundaryTo G S₂ S₁).card ≤ b ∧\n      BisectionTreeMax S₁ bs k ∧ BisectionTreeMax S₂ bs k\n\n@[simp] theorem bisectionTree_nil (S : Finset V) (k : ℕ) :\n    BisectionTree G S [] k ↔ pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) ≤ k := Iff.rfl\n\ntheorem bisectionTree_cons (S : Finset V) (b : ℕ) (bs : List ℕ) (k : ℕ) :\n    BisectionTree G S (b :: bs) k ↔ ∃ S₁ S₂ : Finset V, S₁ ∪ S₂ = S ∧ Disjoint S₁ S₂ ∧\n      min (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card (boundaryTo G S₂ S₁).card ≤ b ∧\n      BisectionTree G S₁ bs k ∧ BisectionTree G S₂ bs k := Iff.rfl\n\n/-- **C2s, relative form.** `BisectionTree G S bs k → pathwidth G[S] ≤ k + bs.sum`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_le_of_bisectionTree :\n    ∀ (bs : List ℕ) (S : Finset V) (k : ℕ), BisectionTree G S bs k →\n      pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) ≤ k + bs.sum\n  | [], S, k, h => by simpa using h\n  | b :: bs, S, k, ⟨S₁, S₂, hS, hd, hb, h₁, h₂⟩ => by\n    have ih₁ := pathwidth_induce_le_of_bisectionTree bs S₁ k h₁\n    have ih₂ := pathwidth_induce_le_of_bisectionTree bs S₂ k h₂\n    have hc := pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_min G S₁ S₂ hd\n    rw [hS] at hc\n    simp only [List.sum_cons]\n    omega\n\n/-- **C2s.** A bisection tree of the whole vertex set with level budgets `bs` and leaf\npathwidth `k` gives `pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTree (bs : List ℕ) (k : ℕ)\n    (h : BisectionTree G Finset.univ bs k) : pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum := by\n  have := pathwidth_induce_le_of_bisectionTree G bs Finset.univ k h\n  rwa [pathwidth_induce_univ] at this\n\n/-- Budgeting the larger boundary budgets the smaller one. -/\ntheorem bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax :\n    ∀ (bs : List ℕ) (S : Finset V) (k : ℕ), BisectionTreeMax G S bs k → BisectionTree G S bs k\n  | [], S, k, h => h\n  | b :: bs, S, k, ⟨S₁, S₂, hS, hd, hb, h₁, h₂⟩ =>\n    ⟨S₁, S₂, hS, hd, le_trans (min_le_max) hb,\n      bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax bs S₁ k h₁, bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax bs S₂ k h₂⟩\n\n/-- **C2 with the larger boundary budgeted**: still `pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax (bs : List ℕ) (k : ℕ)\n    (h : BisectionTreeMax G Finset.univ bs k) : pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum :=\n  pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTree G bs k (bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax G bs _ k h)\n\n/-- **C2, the item's form**: `pathwidth G ≤ k + 2 bs.sum` when every level-`i` split has both\nboundaries of size at most `bs[i]`. The factor 2 is slack (`pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax`). -/\ntheorem pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax_two_mul (bs : List ℕ) (k : ℕ)\n    (h : BisectionTreeMax G Finset.univ bs k) : pathwidth G ≤ k + 2 * bs.sum := by\n  have := pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax G bs k h\n  omega\n\nend MOSPFormalization\nEOF\ncat reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/04_cut/nohup.out","description":"Write CutLemma.lean; peek at the check's progress"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4755,"cache_read_input_tokens":152591,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":4755,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":7,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9391627-7973-489b-a3e2-64b9c429644d","uuid":"23006b58-eaf4-4247-bf5a-f2b988a661aa","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:31:54.370Z","request_id":"req_011CgdKFgs5sxUNdwaeV2PRh","wire_tool_inputs":{"toolu_018Udf7t4cytsh5QxbTxENeW":{"command":"cd /home/al/dev/MOSP && cat > lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/CutLemma.lean <<'EOF'\n/-\nCopyright (c) 2026 Alexandre Linhares. All rights reserved.\nReleased under the MIT license as described in the file LICENSE.\n\n# The cut lemma and its iterated form\n\nItem 04 of loop0012 (`reports/edwards_mcdermid_plan.md` §0.4 (3), §0.5;\n`reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §2.1 (2) and §4): the one-cut transfer — a vertex\npartition with its two boundaries bounds the pathwidth of the whole by the\npathwidths of the two sides — and its recursive iteration. Neither depends on\nthe two named hypotheses of the Edwards–McDermid formalisation\n(`CubicPathwidthBound`, `ReductionPathwidthBound`, item 09); both are tools for\nevery graph.\n\n* `boundaryTo G A B` — the vertices of `A` with a neighbour in `B`;\n  `boundary G A` — the vertices of `A` with a neighbour outside `A`\n  (`boundary_eq_boundaryTo_compl`).\n* `pathwidth_induce_mono` — `T ⊆ U → pathwidth G[T] ≤ pathwidth G[U]`.\n* `pathwidth_induce_le_induce_add_card_sdiff` — `T ⊆ U → pathwidth G[U] ≤ pathwidth G[T] + |U ∖ T|`,\n  the relative form of `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl` (`TreeBound.lean`).\n* `pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_boundaryTo` — for disjoint `S₁`, `S₂`,\n  `pathwidth G[S₁ ∪ S₂] ≤ max (pathwidth G[S₁]) (pathwidth G[S₂]) + |∂(S₁ → S₂)|`:\n  delete the boundary (the lemma above), the rest is a disjoint union with no edge\n  between the sides (`pathwidth_induce_union_le_max`), and `G[S₁ ∖ ∂] ≤ G[S₁]`.\n* **C1s** `pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_min` (relative) and\n  `pathwidth_le_max_add_min_boundary` (global): the separator form\n  `pathwidth G ≤ max (pathwidth G[S]) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ]) + min |∂S| |∂Sᶜ|`.\n* **C1** `pathwidth_le_cut`: the item's three-term form\n  `pathwidth G ≤ max (max (pathwidth G[S] + |∂S|) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ] + |∂Sᶜ|)) (|∂S| + |∂Sᶜ| − 1)`,\n  a corollary of C1s (`max a b + min c d ≤ max (a + c) (b + d)`); stated as the\n  item asks, with the `− 1` in `ℕ`.\n* **C2s** `BisectionTree G S bs k` — a recursive bisection of `S` given level by level:\n  `bs = []` means `pathwidth G[S] ≤ k`; `bs = b :: bs'` means `S` splits into two\n  disjoint parts whose smaller boundary (`min`) has at most `b` vertices, each part\n  carrying a `BisectionTree` for `bs'`. `pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTree`:\n  `BisectionTree G univ bs k → pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum`; by induction on `bs` through\n  the relative C1s, so it never needs a nested `induce`.\n* **C2** `BisectionTreeMax` is the same with the larger boundary (`max`) budgeted, as the\n  item's text has it; it implies `BisectionTree` (`bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax`),\n  and `pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax_two_mul` is the item's `pathwidth G ≤ k + 2 bs.sum`\n  (the factor 2 is slack: `pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax` has `k + bs.sum`).\n\n**What these lemmas do not give.** Fomin & Høie (2006) reach `pw ≤ (1/6 + ε) n` for\ncubic graphs with **one** level — a Monien–Preis bisection with at most `(1/6 + ε/2) n`\ncut edges, their Lemma 4 on each side (a path decomposition of a graph of maximum degree\n3 of width at most `max{|X|, n/3 + 1} + (2/3) log₃ n + 1` whose *last* bag is a\nprescribed set `X`), and a sweep across the boundary that holds the middle bags at\n`|∂V₁| + 1` — not by iterating C2: iterating C2s with Monien–Preis cuts of `(1/6 + ε)`\nof each piece sums to `n/3`. Lemma 4 and the sweep are stated in\n`reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §4 and are not proved here.\n\nEvery statement was checked by brute force before it was stated\n(`reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/04_cut/check.py`): the relative forms on every\nordered pair of disjoint vertex sets of every graph to 7 vertices, the global forms on\nevery partition, the bisection forms on 2,000 random graphs at 10–12 vertices.\n-/\nimport MOSPFormalization.TreeBound\nimport MOSPFormalization.Minor\n\nset_option linter.unusedSectionVars false\n\nnamespace MOSPFormalization\n\nvariable {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]\nvariable (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]\n\n/-! ### Boundaries -/\n\n/-- The vertices of `A` with a neighbour in `B`. -/\ndef boundaryTo (A B : Finset V) : Finset V := A.filter (fun a => ∃ b ∈ B, G.Adj a b)\n\n/-- The boundary of `A`: the vertices of `A` with a neighbour outside `A`. -/\ndef boundary (A : Finset V) : Finset V := A.filter (fun a => ∃ b, b ∉ A ∧ G.Adj a b)\n\ntheorem boundaryTo_subset (A B : Finset V) : boundaryTo G A B ⊆ A := Finset.filter_subset _ _\n\ntheorem boundary_subset (A : Finset V) : boundary G A ⊆ A := Finset.filter_subset _ _\n\ntheorem mem_boundaryTo {A B : Finset V} {a : V} :\n    a ∈ boundaryTo G A B ↔ a ∈ A ∧ ∃ b ∈ B, G.Adj a b := Finset.mem_filter\n\ntheorem mem_boundary {A : Finset V} {a : V} :\n    a ∈ boundary G A ↔ a ∈ A ∧ ∃ b, b ∉ A ∧ G.Adj a b := Finset.mem_filter\n\n/-- The boundary of `A` is its boundary towards the complement. -/\ntheorem boundary_eq_boundaryTo_compl (A : Finset V) : boundary G A = boundaryTo G A Aᶜ := by\n  ext a\n  simp [mem_boundary, mem_boundaryTo]\n\n/-- No edge leaves `A ∖ ∂(A → B)` for `B`. -/\ntheorem not_adj_of_mem_sdiff_boundaryTo {A B : Finset V} {a b : V}\n    (ha : a ∈ A \\ boundaryTo G A B) (hb : b ∈ B) : ¬ G.Adj a b := fun h =>\n  (Finset.mem_sdiff.mp ha).2 ((mem_boundaryTo G).mpr ⟨(Finset.mem_sdiff.mp ha).1, b, hb, h⟩)\n\n/-! ### Induced subgraphs of induced subgraphs -/\n\n/-- Monotonicity under vertex inclusion: `T ⊆ U → pathwidth G[T] ≤ pathwidth G[U]`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_mono {T U : Finset V} (h : T ⊆ U) :\n    pathwidth (G.induce (↑T : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (G.induce (↑U : Set V)) :=\n  pathwidth_le_of_injective (G.induceHomOfLE (Finset.coe_subset.mpr h)).toHom\n    (G.induceHomOfLE (Finset.coe_subset.mpr h)).injective\n\n/-- The pathwidth of `G` is that of `G[univ]`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_univ : pathwidth (G.induce (↑(Finset.univ : Finset V) : Set V)) = pathwidth G := by\n  rw [Finset.coe_univ]\n  exact pathwidth_eq_of_iso (SimpleGraph.induceUnivIso G)\n\n/-- The relative deletion lemma: `T ⊆ U → pathwidth G[U] ≤ pathwidth G[T] + |U ∖ T|`\n(`pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl` applied inside `G[U]`). -/\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_le_induce_add_card_sdiff {T U : Finset V} (h : T ⊆ U) :\n    pathwidth (G.induce (↑U : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (G.induce (↑T : Set V)) + (U \\ T).card := by\n  -- the vertices of `G[U]` that lie in `T`\n  let S : Finset (↑(↑U : Set V)) := Finset.univ.filter (fun x => x.val ∈ T)\n  have h1 := pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl (G.induce (↑U : Set V)) S\n  -- `G[U][S]` embeds in `G[T]`\n  have h2 : pathwidth ((G.induce (↑U : Set V)).induce (↑S : Set ↑(↑U : Set V))) ≤\n      pathwidth (G.induce (↑T : Set V)) := by\n    refine pathwidth_le_of_injective\n      (⟨fun x => ⟨x.val.val, (Finset.mem_filter.mp (Finset.mem_coe.mp x.2)).2⟩,\n        fun {x y} hxy => hxy⟩ : (G.induce (↑U : Set V)).induce (↑S : Set ↑(↑U : Set V)) →g\n          G.induce (↑T : Set V)) ?_\n    intro x y hxy\n    exact Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext (congrArg Subtype.val hxy))\n  -- the complement of `S` in `G[U]` injects into `U ∖ T`\n  have h3 : Sᶜ.card ≤ (U \\ T).card := by\n    refine Finset.card_le_card_of_injOn (fun x => x.val) ?_ Subtype.val_injective.injOn\n    intro x hx\n    have hx' := Finset.mem_compl.mp hx\n    simp only [S, Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and] at hx'\n    exact Finset.mem_sdiff.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_coe.mp x.2, hx'⟩\n  omega\n\n/-! ### C1s: the separator form of the cut lemma -/\n\n/-- One side of the cut lemma: for disjoint `S₁`, `S₂`,\n`pathwidth G[S₁ ∪ S₂] ≤ max (pathwidth G[S₁]) (pathwidth G[S₂]) + |∂(S₁ → S₂)|`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_boundaryTo (S₁ S₂ : Finset V) (hd : Disjoint S₁ S₂) :\n    pathwidth (G.induce (↑(S₁ ∪ S₂) : Set V)) ≤\n      max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₁ : Set V))) (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₂ : Set V))) +\n        (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card := by\n  set B := boundaryTo G S₁ S₂ with hB\n  set T := (S₁ \\ B) ∪ S₂ with hT\n  have hTU : T ⊆ S₁ ∪ S₂ :=\n    Finset.union_subset_union Finset.sdiff_subset (Finset.Subset.refl _)\n  -- delete the boundary: at most `|B|` vertices\n  have h1 := pathwidth_induce_le_induce_add_card_sdiff G hTU\n  have hcard : ((S₁ ∪ S₂) \\ T).card ≤ B.card := by\n    apply Finset.card_le_card\n    intro x hx\n    simp only [hT, Finset.mem_sdiff, Finset.mem_union, not_or, not_and, not_not] at hx\n    rcases hx.1 with h | h\n    · exact hx.2.1 h\n    · exact absurd h hx.2.2\n  -- the rest is a disjoint union with no edge between the sides\n  have h2 : pathwidth (G.induce (↑T : Set V)) ≤\n      max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑(S₁ \\ B) : Set V))) (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₂ : Set V))) :=\n    pathwidth_induce_union_le_max G (S₁ \\ B) S₂\n      (Finset.disjoint_of_subset_left Finset.sdiff_subset hd)\n      (fun a ha b hb => not_adj_of_mem_sdiff_boundaryTo G ha hb)\n  have h3 : pathwidth (G.induce (↑(S₁ \\ B) : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₁ : Set V)) :=\n    pathwidth_induce_mono G Finset.sdiff_subset\n  omega\n\n/-- **C1s, relative form.** For disjoint `S₁`, `S₂`,\n`pathwidth G[S₁ ∪ S₂] ≤ max (pathwidth G[S₁]) (pathwidth G[S₂]) + min |∂(S₁ → S₂)| |∂(S₂ → S₁)|`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_min (S₁ S₂ : Finset V) (hd : Disjoint S₁ S₂) :\n    pathwidth (G.induce (↑(S₁ ∪ S₂) : Set V)) ≤\n      max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₁ : Set V))) (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₂ : Set V))) +\n        min (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card (boundaryTo G S₂ S₁).card := by\n  have h1 := pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_boundaryTo G S₁ S₂ hd\n  have h2 := pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_boundaryTo G S₂ S₁ hd.symm\n  rw [Finset.union_comm] at h2\n  omega\n\n/-- **C1s.** `pathwidth G ≤ max (pathwidth G[S]) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ]) + min |∂S| |∂Sᶜ|`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_le_max_add_min_boundary (S : Finset V) :\n    pathwidth G ≤\n      max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V))) (pathwidth (G.induce (↑Sᶜ : Set V))) +\n        min (boundary G S).card (boundary G Sᶜ).card := by\n  have h := pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_min G S Sᶜ Finset.disjoint_compl_right\n  rw [Finset.union_compl, pathwidth_induce_univ] at h\n  rw [boundary_eq_boundaryTo_compl, boundary_eq_boundaryTo_compl, compl_compl]\n  exact h\n\n/-- **C1**, the item's three-term form:\n`pathwidth G ≤ max (max (pathwidth G[S] + |∂S|) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ] + |∂Sᶜ|)) (|∂S| + |∂Sᶜ| − 1)`.\nThe last term is never the binding one; it is kept because Fomin & Høie's\n`P₁, P₂, P₃` construction has it. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_le_cut (S : Finset V) :\n    pathwidth G ≤\n      max (max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) + (boundary G S).card)\n               (pathwidth (G.induce (↑Sᶜ : Set V)) + (boundary G Sᶜ).card))\n          ((boundary G S).card + (boundary G Sᶜ).card - 1) := by\n  have h := pathwidth_le_max_add_min_boundary G S\n  omega\n\n/-! ### C2: the iterated form -/\n\n/-- A recursive bisection of `S`, level by level: `BisectionTree G S [] k` says\n`pathwidth G[S] ≤ k`; `BisectionTree G S (b :: bs) k` says `S` is the disjoint union of\ntwo parts whose smaller boundary has at most `b` vertices, each a `BisectionTree` for\n`bs`. -/\ndef BisectionTree : Finset V → List ℕ → ℕ → Prop\n  | S, [], k => pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) ≤ k\n  | S, b :: bs, k => ∃ S₁ S₂ : Finset V, S₁ ∪ S₂ = S ∧ Disjoint S₁ S₂ ∧\n      min (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card (boundaryTo G S₂ S₁).card ≤ b ∧\n      BisectionTree S₁ bs k ∧ BisectionTree S₂ bs k\n\n/-- The same with the larger boundary budgeted at each split (the item's C2). -/\ndef BisectionTreeMax : Finset V → List ℕ → ℕ → Prop\n  | S, [], k => pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) ≤ k\n  | S, b :: bs, k => ∃ S₁ S₂ : Finset V, S₁ ∪ S₂ = S ∧ Disjoint S₁ S₂ ∧\n      max (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card (boundaryTo G S₂ S₁).card ≤ b ∧\n      BisectionTreeMax S₁ bs k ∧ BisectionTreeMax S₂ bs k\n\n@[simp] theorem bisectionTree_nil (S : Finset V) (k : ℕ) :\n    BisectionTree G S [] k ↔ pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) ≤ k := Iff.rfl\n\ntheorem bisectionTree_cons (S : Finset V) (b : ℕ) (bs : List ℕ) (k : ℕ) :\n    BisectionTree G S (b :: bs) k ↔ ∃ S₁ S₂ : Finset V, S₁ ∪ S₂ = S ∧ Disjoint S₁ S₂ ∧\n      min (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card (boundaryTo G S₂ S₁).card ≤ b ∧\n      BisectionTree G S₁ bs k ∧ BisectionTree G S₂ bs k := Iff.rfl\n\n/-- **C2s, relative form.** `BisectionTree G S bs k → pathwidth G[S] ≤ k + bs.sum`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_induce_le_of_bisectionTree :\n    ∀ (bs : List ℕ) (S : Finset V) (k : ℕ), BisectionTree G S bs k →\n      pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) ≤ k + bs.sum\n  | [], S, k, h => by simpa using h\n  | b :: bs, S, k, ⟨S₁, S₂, hS, hd, hb, h₁, h₂⟩ => by\n    have ih₁ := pathwidth_induce_le_of_bisectionTree bs S₁ k h₁\n    have ih₂ := pathwidth_induce_le_of_bisectionTree bs S₂ k h₂\n    have hc := pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_min G S₁ S₂ hd\n    rw [hS] at hc\n    simp only [List.sum_cons]\n    omega\n\n/-- **C2s.** A bisection tree of the whole vertex set with level budgets `bs` and leaf\npathwidth `k` gives `pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTree (bs : List ℕ) (k : ℕ)\n    (h : BisectionTree G Finset.univ bs k) : pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum := by\n  have := pathwidth_induce_le_of_bisectionTree G bs Finset.univ k h\n  rwa [pathwidth_induce_univ] at this\n\n/-- Budgeting the larger boundary budgets the smaller one. -/\ntheorem bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax :\n    ∀ (bs : List ℕ) (S : Finset V) (k : ℕ), BisectionTreeMax G S bs k → BisectionTree G S bs k\n  | [], S, k, h => h\n  | b :: bs, S, k, ⟨S₁, S₂, hS, hd, hb, h₁, h₂⟩ =>\n    ⟨S₁, S₂, hS, hd, le_trans (min_le_max) hb,\n      bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax bs S₁ k h₁, bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax bs S₂ k h₂⟩\n\n/-- **C2 with the larger boundary budgeted**: still `pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum`. -/\ntheorem pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax (bs : List ℕ) (k : ℕ)\n    (h : BisectionTreeMax G Finset.univ bs k) : pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum :=\n  pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTree G bs k (bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax G bs _ k h)\n\n/-- **C2, the item's form**: `pathwidth G ≤ k + 2 bs.sum` when every level-`i` split has both\nboundaries of size at most `bs[i]`. The factor 2 is slack (`pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax`). -/\ntheorem pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax_two_mul (bs : List ℕ) (k : ℕ)\n    (h : BisectionTreeMax G Finset.univ bs k) : pathwidth G ≤ k + 2 * bs.sum := by\n  have := pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax G bs k h\n  omega\n\nend MOSPFormalization\nEOF\ncat reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/04_cut/nohup.out","description":"Write CutLemma.lean; peek at the check's progress"}},"wire_ingest_context":{"toolu_018Udf7t4cytsh5QxbTxENeW":{"cwd":"/home/al/dev/MOSP"}}}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018Udf7t4cytsh5QxbTxENeW","type":"tool_result","content":"# item 04 brute-force check, 2026-11-02 02:30:38 UTC, n = 1..7, 8 workers, part B seed 4\nn=1: 1 graphs in 0.0s; C1=1; C1r=3; C1r1=3; C1s=1; C1s_tight=1; L1r=3; M=3; C1s slack 0:1\nn=2: 2 graphs in 0.0s; C1=4; C1r=18; C1r1=18; C1s=4; C1s_tight=4; L1r=18; M=18; C1s slack 0:4\nn=3: 4 graphs in 0.0s; C1=16; C1r=108; C1r1=108; C1s=16; C1s_tight=14; L1r=108; M=108; C1s slack 0:14, 1:2\nn=4: 11 graphs in 0.0s; C1=88; C1r=891; C1r1=891; C1s=88; C1s_tight=55; L1r=891; M=891; C1s slack 0:55, 1:32, 2:1\nn=5: 34 graphs in 0.0s; C1=544; C1r=8262; C1r1=8262; C1s=544; C1s_tight=247; L1r=8262; M=8262; C1s slack 0:247, 1:268, 2:29\nn=6: 156 graphs in 0.0s; C1=4992; C1r=113724; C1r1=113724; C1s=4992; C1s_tight=1503; L1r=113724; M=113724; C1s slack 0:1503, 1:2590, 2:875, 3:24\nn=7: 1044 graphs in 0.5s; C1=66816; C1r=2283228; C1r1=2283228; C1s=66816; C1s_tight=13235; L1r=2283228; M=2283228; C1s slack 0:13235, 1:33417, 2:18868, 3:1296\npart B slack of C2s (k + Σ b − pw): 0:20, 1:178, 2:1545, 3:3078, 4:3102, 5:1642, 6:392, 7:42, 8:1\npart B: 2000 random graphs at n = 10, 11, 12 in 4.4s; C2=10000; C2m=10000; C2s=10000\ndone in 5.0s; violations: 0","is_error":false}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"d9391627-7973-489b-a3e2-64b9c429644d","uuid":"1b84e7c4-7fdc-489a-a264-5293eeb0c431","timestamp":"2026-11-02T02:31:54.391Z","tool_use_result":{"stdout":"# item 04 brute-force check, 2026-11-02 02:30:38 UTC, n = 1..7, 8 workers, part B seed 4\nn=1: 1 graphs in 0.0s; C1=1; C1r=3; C1r1=3; C1s=1; C1s_tight=1; L1r=3; M=3; C1s slack 0:1\nn=2: 2 graphs in 0.0s; C1=4; C1r=18; C1r1=18; C1s=4; C1s_tight=4; L1r=18; M=18; C1s slack 0:4\nn=3: 4 graphs in 0.0s; C1=16; C1r=108; C1r1=108; C1s=16; C1s_tight=14; L1r=108; M=108; C1s slack 0:14, 1:2\nn=4: 11 graphs in 0.0s; C1=88; C1r=891; C1r1=891; C1s=88; C1s_tight=55; L1r=891; M=891; C1s slack 0:55, 1:32, 2:1\nn=5: 34 graphs in 0.0s; C1=544; C1r=8262; C1r1=8262; C1s=544; C1s_tight=247; L1r=8262; M=8262; C1s slack 0:247, 1:268, 2:29\nn=6: 156 graphs in 0.0s; C1=4992; C1r=113724; C1r1=113724; C1s=4992; C1s_tight=1503; L1r=113724; M=113724; C1s slack 0:1503, 1:2590, 2:875, 3:24\nn=7: 1044 graphs in 0.5s; C1=66816; C1r=2283228; C1r1=2283228; C1s=66816; C1s_tight=13235; L1r=2283228; M=2283228; C1s slack 0:13235, 1:33417, 2:18868, 3:1296\npart B slack of C2s (k + Σ b − pw): 0:20, 1:178, 2:1545, 3:3078, 4:3102, 5:1642, 6:392, 7:42, 8:1\npart B: 2000 random graphs at n = 10, 11, 12 in 4.4s; C2=10000; C2m=10000; C2s=10000\ndone in 5.0s; violations: 0","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false,"bashEditDiff":{"files":[{"filePath":"/home/al/dev/MOSP/lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/CutLemma.lean","hunks":[{"oldStart":1,"oldLines":0,"newStart":1,"newLines":264,"lines":["+/-","+Copyright (c) 2026 Alexandre Linhares. All rights reserved.","+Released under the MIT license as described in the file LICENSE.","+","+# The cut lemma and its iterated form","+","+Item 04 of loop0012 (`reports/edwards_mcdermid_plan.md` §0.4 (3), §0.5;","+`reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §2.1 (2) and §4): the one-cut transfer — a vertex","+partition with its two boundaries bounds the pathwidth of the whole by the","+pathwidths of the two sides — and its recursive iteration. Neither depends on","+the two named hypotheses of the Edwards–McDermid formalisation","+(`CubicPathwidthBound`, `ReductionPathwidthBound`, item 09); both are tools for","+every graph.","+","+* `boundaryTo G A B` — the vertices of `A` with a neighbour in `B`;","+  `boundary G A` — the vertices of `A` with a neighbour outside `A`","+  (`boundary_eq_boundaryTo_compl`).","+* `pathwidth_induce_mono` — `T ⊆ U → pathwidth G[T] ≤ pathwidth G[U]`.","+* `pathwidth_induce_le_induce_add_card_sdiff` — `T ⊆ U → pathwidth G[U] ≤ pathwidth G[T] + |U ∖ T|`,","+  the relative form of `pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl` (`TreeBound.lean`).","+* `pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_boundaryTo` — for disjoint `S₁`, `S₂`,","+  `pathwidth G[S₁ ∪ S₂] ≤ max (pathwidth G[S₁]) (pathwidth G[S₂]) + |∂(S₁ → S₂)|`:","+  delete the boundary (the lemma above), the rest is a disjoint union with no edge","+  between the sides (`pathwidth_induce_union_le_max`), and `G[S₁ ∖ ∂] ≤ G[S₁]`.","+* **C1s** `pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_min` (relative) and","+  `pathwidth_le_max_add_min_boundary` (global): the separator form","+  `pathwidth G ≤ max (pathwidth G[S]) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ]) + min |∂S| |∂Sᶜ|`.","+* **C1** `pathwidth_le_cut`: the item's three-term form","+  `pathwidth G ≤ max (max (pathwidth G[S] + |∂S|) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ] + |∂Sᶜ|)) (|∂S| + |∂Sᶜ| − 1)`,","+  a corollary of C1s (`max a b + min c d ≤ max (a + c) (b + d)`); stated as the","+  item asks, with the `− 1` in `ℕ`.","+* **C2s** `BisectionTree G S bs k` — a recursive bisection of `S` given level by level:","+  `bs = []` means `pathwidth G[S] ≤ k`; `bs = b :: bs'` means `S` splits into two","+  disjoint parts whose smaller boundary (`min`) has at most `b` vertices, each part","+  carrying a `BisectionTree` for `bs'`. `pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTree`:","+  `BisectionTree G univ bs k → pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum`; by induction on `bs` through","+  the relative C1s, so it never needs a nested `induce`.","+* **C2** `BisectionTreeMax` is the same with the larger boundary (`max`) budgeted, as the","+  item's text has it; it implies `BisectionTree` (`bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax`),","+  and `pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax_two_mul` is the item's `pathwidth G ≤ k + 2 bs.sum`","+  (the factor 2 is slack: `pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax` has `k + bs.sum`).","+","+**What these lemmas do not give.** Fomin & Høie (2006) reach `pw ≤ (1/6 + ε) n` for","+cubic graphs with **one** level — a Monien–Preis bisection with at most `(1/6 + ε/2) n`","+cut edges, their Lemma 4 on each side (a path decomposition of a graph of maximum degree","+3 of width at most `max{|X|, n/3 + 1} + (2/3) log₃ n + 1` whose *last* bag is a","+prescribed set `X`), and a sweep across the boundary that holds the middle bags at","+`|∂V₁| + 1` — not by iterating C2: iterating C2s with Monien–Preis cuts of `(1/6 + ε)`","+of each piece sums to `n/3`. Lemma 4 and the sweep are stated in","+`reports/edwards_mcdermid.md` §4 and are not proved here.","+","+Every statement was checked by brute force before it was stated","+(`reports/scratch/edwards_mcdermid/04_cut/check.py`): the relative forms on every","+ordered pair of disjoint vertex sets of every graph to 7 vertices, the global forms on","+every partition, the bisection forms on 2,000 random graphs at 10–12 vertices.","+-/","+import MOSPFormalization.TreeBound","+import MOSPFormalization.Minor","+","+set_option linter.unusedSectionVars false","+","+namespace MOSPFormalization","+","+variable {V : Type*} [Fintype V] [DecidableEq V]","+variable (G : SimpleGraph V) [DecidableRel G.Adj]","+","+/-! ### Boundaries -/","+","+/-- The vertices of `A` with a neighbour in `B`. -/","+def boundaryTo (A B : Finset V) : Finset V := A.filter (fun a => ∃ b ∈ B, G.Adj a b)","+","+/-- The boundary of `A`: the vertices of `A` with a neighbour outside `A`. -/","+def boundary (A : Finset V) : Finset V := A.filter (fun a => ∃ b, b ∉ A ∧ G.Adj a b)","+","+theorem boundaryTo_subset (A B : Finset V) : boundaryTo G A B ⊆ A := Finset.filter_subset _ _","+","+theorem boundary_subset (A : Finset V) : boundary G A ⊆ A := Finset.filter_subset _ _","+","+theorem mem_boundaryTo {A B : Finset V} {a : V} :","+    a ∈ boundaryTo G A B ↔ a ∈ A ∧ ∃ b ∈ B, G.Adj a b := Finset.mem_filter","+","+theorem mem_boundary {A : Finset V} {a : V} :","+    a ∈ boundary G A ↔ a ∈ A ∧ ∃ b, b ∉ A ∧ G.Adj a b := Finset.mem_filter","+","+/-- The boundary of `A` is its boundary towards the complement. -/","+theorem boundary_eq_boundaryTo_compl (A : Finset V) : boundary G A = boundaryTo G A Aᶜ := by","+  ext a","+  simp [mem_boundary, mem_boundaryTo]","+","+/-- No edge leaves `A ∖ ∂(A → B)` for `B`. -/","+theorem not_adj_of_mem_sdiff_boundaryTo {A B : Finset V} {a b : V}","+    (ha : a ∈ A \\ boundaryTo G A B) (hb : b ∈ B) : ¬ G.Adj a b := fun h =>","+  (Finset.mem_sdiff.mp ha).2 ((mem_boundaryTo G).mpr ⟨(Finset.mem_sdiff.mp ha).1, b, hb, h⟩)","+","+/-! ### Induced subgraphs of induced subgraphs -/","+","+/-- Monotonicity under vertex inclusion: `T ⊆ U → pathwidth G[T] ≤ pathwidth G[U]`. -/","+theorem pathwidth_induce_mono {T U : Finset V} (h : T ⊆ U) :","+    pathwidth (G.induce (↑T : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (G.induce (↑U : Set V)) :=","+  pathwidth_le_of_injective (G.induceHomOfLE (Finset.coe_subset.mpr h)).toHom","+    (G.induceHomOfLE (Finset.coe_subset.mpr h)).injective","+","+/-- The pathwidth of `G` is that of `G[univ]`. -/","+theorem pathwidth_induce_univ : pathwidth (G.induce (↑(Finset.univ : Finset V) : Set V)) = pathwidth G := by","+  rw [Finset.coe_univ]","+  exact pathwidth_eq_of_iso (SimpleGraph.induceUnivIso G)","+","+/-- The relative deletion lemma: `T ⊆ U → pathwidth G[U] ≤ pathwidth G[T] + |U ∖ T|`","+(`pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl` applied inside `G[U]`). -/","+theorem pathwidth_induce_le_induce_add_card_sdiff {T U : Finset V} (h : T ⊆ U) :","+    pathwidth (G.induce (↑U : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (G.induce (↑T : Set V)) + (U \\ T).card := by","+  -- the vertices of `G[U]` that lie in `T`","+  let S : Finset (↑(↑U : Set V)) := Finset.univ.filter (fun x => x.val ∈ T)","+  have h1 := pathwidth_le_pathwidth_induce_add_card_compl (G.induce (↑U : Set V)) S","+  -- `G[U][S]` embeds in `G[T]`","+  have h2 : pathwidth ((G.induce (↑U : Set V)).induce (↑S : Set ↑(↑U : Set V))) ≤","+      pathwidth (G.induce (↑T : Set V)) := by","+    refine pathwidth_le_of_injective","+      (⟨fun x => ⟨x.val.val, (Finset.mem_filter.mp (Finset.mem_coe.mp x.2)).2⟩,","+        fun {x y} hxy => hxy⟩ : (G.induce (↑U : Set V)).induce (↑S : Set ↑(↑U : Set V)) →g","+          G.induce (↑T : Set V)) ?_","+    intro x y hxy","+    exact Subtype.ext (Subtype.ext (congrArg Subtype.val hxy))","+  -- the complement of `S` in `G[U]` injects into `U ∖ T`","+  have h3 : Sᶜ.card ≤ (U \\ T).card := by","+    refine Finset.card_le_card_of_injOn (fun x => x.val) ?_ Subtype.val_injective.injOn","+    intro x hx","+    have hx' := Finset.mem_compl.mp hx","+    simp only [S, Finset.mem_filter, Finset.mem_univ, true_and] at hx'","+    exact Finset.mem_sdiff.mpr ⟨Finset.mem_coe.mp x.2, hx'⟩","+  omega","+","+/-! ### C1s: the separator form of the cut lemma -/","+","+/-- One side of the cut lemma: for disjoint `S₁`, `S₂`,","+`pathwidth G[S₁ ∪ S₂] ≤ max (pathwidth G[S₁]) (pathwidth G[S₂]) + |∂(S₁ → S₂)|`. -/","+theorem pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_boundaryTo (S₁ S₂ : Finset V) (hd : Disjoint S₁ S₂) :","+    pathwidth (G.induce (↑(S₁ ∪ S₂) : Set V)) ≤","+      max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₁ : Set V))) (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₂ : Set V))) +","+        (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card := by","+  set B := boundaryTo G S₁ S₂ with hB","+  set T := (S₁ \\ B) ∪ S₂ with hT","+  have hTU : T ⊆ S₁ ∪ S₂ :=","+    Finset.union_subset_union Finset.sdiff_subset (Finset.Subset.refl _)","+  -- delete the boundary: at most `|B|` vertices","+  have h1 := pathwidth_induce_le_induce_add_card_sdiff G hTU","+  have hcard : ((S₁ ∪ S₂) \\ T).card ≤ B.card := by","+    apply Finset.card_le_card","+    intro x hx","+    simp only [hT, Finset.mem_sdiff, Finset.mem_union, not_or, not_and, not_not] at hx","+    rcases hx.1 with h | h","+    · exact hx.2.1 h","+    · exact absurd h hx.2.2","+  -- the rest is a disjoint union with no edge between the sides","+  have h2 : pathwidth (G.induce (↑T : Set V)) ≤","+      max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑(S₁ \\ B) : Set V))) (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₂ : Set V))) :=","+    pathwidth_induce_union_le_max G (S₁ \\ B) S₂","+      (Finset.disjoint_of_subset_left Finset.sdiff_subset hd)","+      (fun a ha b hb => not_adj_of_mem_sdiff_boundaryTo G ha hb)","+  have h3 : pathwidth (G.induce (↑(S₁ \\ B) : Set V)) ≤ pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₁ : Set V)) :=","+    pathwidth_induce_mono G Finset.sdiff_subset","+  omega","+","+/-- **C1s, relative form.** For disjoint `S₁`, `S₂`,","+`pathwidth G[S₁ ∪ S₂] ≤ max (pathwidth G[S₁]) (pathwidth G[S₂]) + min |∂(S₁ → S₂)| |∂(S₂ → S₁)|`. -/","+theorem pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_min (S₁ S₂ : Finset V) (hd : Disjoint S₁ S₂) :","+    pathwidth (G.induce (↑(S₁ ∪ S₂) : Set V)) ≤","+      max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₁ : Set V))) (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S₂ : Set V))) +","+        min (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card (boundaryTo G S₂ S₁).card := by","+  have h1 := pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_boundaryTo G S₁ S₂ hd","+  have h2 := pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_boundaryTo G S₂ S₁ hd.symm","+  rw [Finset.union_comm] at h2","+  omega","+","+/-- **C1s.** `pathwidth G ≤ max (pathwidth G[S]) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ]) + min |∂S| |∂Sᶜ|`. -/","+theorem pathwidth_le_max_add_min_boundary (S : Finset V) :","+    pathwidth G ≤","+      max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V))) (pathwidth (G.induce (↑Sᶜ : Set V))) +","+        min (boundary G S).card (boundary G Sᶜ).card := by","+  have h := pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_min G S Sᶜ Finset.disjoint_compl_right","+  rw [Finset.union_compl, pathwidth_induce_univ] at h","+  rw [boundary_eq_boundaryTo_compl, boundary_eq_boundaryTo_compl, compl_compl]","+  exact h","+","+/-- **C1**, the item's three-term form:","+`pathwidth G ≤ max (max (pathwidth G[S] + |∂S|) (pathwidth G[Sᶜ] + |∂Sᶜ|)) (|∂S| + |∂Sᶜ| − 1)`.","+The last term is never the binding one; it is kept because Fomin & Høie's","+`P₁, P₂, P₃` construction has it. -/","+theorem pathwidth_le_cut (S : Finset V) :","+    pathwidth G ≤","+      max (max (pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) + (boundary G S).card)","+               (pathwidth (G.induce (↑Sᶜ : Set V)) + (boundary G Sᶜ).card))","+          ((boundary G S).card + (boundary G Sᶜ).card - 1) := by","+  have h := pathwidth_le_max_add_min_boundary G S","+  omega","+","+/-! ### C2: the iterated form -/","+","+/-- A recursive bisection of `S`, level by level: `BisectionTree G S [] k` says","+`pathwidth G[S] ≤ k`; `BisectionTree G S (b :: bs) k` says `S` is the disjoint union of","+two parts whose smaller boundary has at most `b` vertices, each a `BisectionTree` for","+`bs`. -/","+def BisectionTree : Finset V → List ℕ → ℕ → Prop","+  | S, [], k => pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) ≤ k","+  | S, b :: bs, k => ∃ S₁ S₂ : Finset V, S₁ ∪ S₂ = S ∧ Disjoint S₁ S₂ ∧","+      min (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card (boundaryTo G S₂ S₁).card ≤ b ∧","+      BisectionTree S₁ bs k ∧ BisectionTree S₂ bs k","+","+/-- The same with the larger boundary budgeted at each split (the item's C2). -/","+def BisectionTreeMax : Finset V → List ℕ → ℕ → Prop","+  | S, [], k => pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) ≤ k","+  | S, b :: bs, k => ∃ S₁ S₂ : Finset V, S₁ ∪ S₂ = S ∧ Disjoint S₁ S₂ ∧","+      max (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card (boundaryTo G S₂ S₁).card ≤ b ∧","+      BisectionTreeMax S₁ bs k ∧ BisectionTreeMax S₂ bs k","+","+@[simp] theorem bisectionTree_nil (S : Finset V) (k : ℕ) :","+    BisectionTree G S [] k ↔ pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) ≤ k := Iff.rfl","+","+theorem bisectionTree_cons (S : Finset V) (b : ℕ) (bs : List ℕ) (k : ℕ) :","+    BisectionTree G S (b :: bs) k ↔ ∃ S₁ S₂ : Finset V, S₁ ∪ S₂ = S ∧ Disjoint S₁ S₂ ∧","+      min (boundaryTo G S₁ S₂).card (boundaryTo G S₂ S₁).card ≤ b ∧","+      BisectionTree G S₁ bs k ∧ BisectionTree G S₂ bs k := Iff.rfl","+","+/-- **C2s, relative form.** `BisectionTree G S bs k → pathwidth G[S] ≤ k + bs.sum`. -/","+theorem pathwidth_induce_le_of_bisectionTree :","+    ∀ (bs : List ℕ) (S : Finset V) (k : ℕ), BisectionTree G S bs k →","+      pathwidth (G.induce (↑S : Set V)) ≤ k + bs.sum","+  | [], S, k, h => by simpa using h","+  | b :: bs, S, k, ⟨S₁, S₂, hS, hd, hb, h₁, h₂⟩ => by","+    have ih₁ := pathwidth_induce_le_of_bisectionTree bs S₁ k h₁","+    have ih₂ := pathwidth_induce_le_of_bisectionTree bs S₂ k h₂","+    have hc := pathwidth_induce_union_le_max_add_min G S₁ S₂ hd","+    rw [hS] at hc","+    simp only [List.sum_cons]","+    omega","+","+/-- **C2s.** A bisection tree of the whole vertex set with level budgets `bs` and leaf","+pathwidth `k` gives `pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum`. -/","+theorem pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTree (bs : List ℕ) (k : ℕ)","+    (h : BisectionTree G Finset.univ bs k) : pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum := by","+  have := pathwidth_induce_le_of_bisectionTree G bs Finset.univ k h","+  rwa [pathwidth_induce_univ] at this","+","+/-- Budgeting the larger boundary budgets the smaller one. -/","+theorem bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax :","+    ∀ (bs : List ℕ) (S : Finset V) (k : ℕ), BisectionTreeMax G S bs k → BisectionTree G S bs k","+  | [], S, k, h => h","+  | b :: bs, S, k, ⟨S₁, S₂, hS, hd, hb, h₁, h₂⟩ =>","+    ⟨S₁, S₂, hS, hd, le_trans (min_le_max) hb,","+      bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax bs S₁ k h₁, bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax bs S₂ k h₂⟩","+","+/-- **C2 with the larger boundary budgeted**: still `pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum`. -/","+theorem pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax (bs : List ℕ) (k : ℕ)","+    (h : BisectionTreeMax G Finset.univ bs k) : pathwidth G ≤ k + bs.sum :=","+  pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTree G bs k (bisectionTree_of_bisectionTreeMax G bs _ k h)","+","+/-- **C2, the item's form**: `pathwidth G ≤ k + 2 bs.sum` when every level-`i` split has both","+boundaries of size at most `bs[i]`. The factor 2 is slack (`pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax`). -/","+theorem pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax_two_mul (bs : List ℕ) (k : ℕ)","+    (h : BisectionTreeMax G Finset.univ bs k) : pathwidth G ≤ k + 2 * bs.sum := by","+  have := pathwidth_le_of_bisectionTreeMax G bs k h","+  omega","+","+end MOSPFormalization"]}],"created":true}],"moreFiles":0,"changedFiles":["/home/al/dev/MOSP/lean/MOSPFormalization/DegreeBound/CutLemma.lean"]}},"tool_result_meta":[{"id":"toolu_018Udf7t4cytsh5QxbTxENeW","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}]}
